{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, of Jeduthun.</b> The beauty of the piyyut is that its beginning is 'of Jeduthun': either Jeduthun the poet composed it, or another composed it about him, for it is a distant instrument."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 62, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:26.909981712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}